{% extends "base.njk" %}
{% block title %}Set Up Open Drawings{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<div class="page-head"><div><h1>Set Up Open Drawings</h1><div class="muted">One time, on each Windows PC that will use the <b>Open Drawings</b> button on a job page.</div></div></div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <p>Open Drawings opens the job's drawings folder in File Explorer: <b>{{ example.path if example else 'G:\\092115-1-1\\003 - PDF PRINTS' }}</b> for job 092115-1-1. A web page cannot open a folder by itself, so this PC needs a small setup first. Until then, <b>Copy Path</b> on the job page copies the folder's address for you to paste into File Explorer.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>It changes <b>this Windows user only</b> (one link type under the current user's settings and one small script in their own profile). No administrator is needed.</li>
    <li>The script can only ever open an existing <b>folder</b> in File Explorer. It checks the job number, drive and folder name in every link, and it never runs a file.</li>
    <li>The drive and folder name come from <a href="/settings#drawings">Settings &gt; Drawings Folder</a>. If they change, nothing needs redoing on the PCs.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Set up this PC</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/tools/folder-button/setup.bat" download>Download the setup file</a></li>
    <li>Open it from your Downloads folder (double-click). If Windows warns about it, choose <b>More info</b> then <b>Run anyway</b>. It is plain text: you can open it in Notepad to read exactly what it does.</li>
    <li>Wait for <b>Done</b>, then press any key.</li>
    <li>On a job page press <b>Open Drawings</b>. The first time, your browser asks to open <b>Uni-Fab Post-Mortem folder</b>: tick <b>Always allow</b> and say yes.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="muted">The drive must be connected on this PC with the same letter ({{ s.drawingsRoot }}). If a job has no <b>{{ s.drawingsFolder }}</b> folder yet, its job folder opens instead, and if there is no job folder, the drive.</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Undo it</h2>
  <p><a class="btn" href="/tools/folder-button/remove.bat" download>Download the remove file</a> and open it the same way. It deletes the link type and the script again. Copy Path keeps working.</p>
</div>
{% endblock %}
